From: Ayman Ragab <aymanrar2c@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 22:36:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Fix video pipeline stop streaming teardown

When switching cameras, video_stop_streaming() walks the full pipeline and
calls s_stream(0) on every subdev. Subdevs that were never started still
have s_stream_enabled == 0, which triggers WARN_ON in the V4L2 subdev core
and can leave the CAMSS graph wedged (front camera black, csiphy EBUSY).

Only stop subdevs that are actually streaming, log errors for real failures,
and continue best-effort teardown instead of returning early.

---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 831486e14754..c4a8f1b2e3a1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -310,11 +310,13 @@ static void video_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 		entity = pad->entity;
 		subdev = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(entity);
 
+		if (!subdev->s_stream_enabled)
+			continue;
+
 		ret = v4l2_subdev_call(subdev, video, s_stream, 0);
-
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(video->camss->dev, "Video pipeline stop failed: %d\n", ret);
-			return;
-		}
+		if (ret && ret != -ENOIOCTLCMD)
+			dev_err(video->camss->dev,
+				"Video pipeline stop failed: %d\n", ret);
  	}
